# tools/qa/check_website_coverage.py hashes the exact bytes of these directories/files to fingerprint
# "user-facing source" for its showcase-drift check, and tools/demo/generate_demo_wip_state.py hashes
# tools/demo/fixtures/*.md byte-for-byte into the committed demo/wip-state-v1.json regression fixture
# (app/backend/wip/content.py's whole_file_hash). Without a forced EOL, core.autocrlf differences
# between platforms (CRLF on a Windows checkout, LF on Linux CI) change those hashed bytes and make
# both fixtures non-reproducible across machines -- confirmed as the cause of two separate CI-only
# failures (test_demo_snapshot.py::test_demo_wip_state_regenerates_from_real_sandbox_deterministically
# and check_website_coverage.py's source_fingerprint mismatch). text=auto lets git's own binary
# detection skip real binaries (e.g. adapters/word/icon.png) that live alongside text files in the
# same glob.
tools/demo/fixtures/*.md text=auto eol=lf

app/frontend/index.html text=auto eol=lf
app/frontend/styles.css text=auto eol=lf
app/frontend/js/*.jsx text=auto eol=lf
app/backend/help/help_content.md text=auto eol=lf
adapters/libreoffice/** text=auto eol=lf
adapters/word/** text=auto eol=lf
adapters/google_docs/** text=auto eol=lf
tui/** text=auto eol=lf
mcp_server/** text=auto eol=lf
